{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities","id":1474669,"title":"Pantheons & Ethnicities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-14T18:26:29-08:00","id":1474669,"title":"Pantheons & Ethnicities","content":"Should I assume that any character from original ethnicity of Panteon is under this Pantheon godly 'jurisdiction'?<br /> <br /> For example, Netjar of Egypt are connected to Middle Eastern people - even if majority of people there are monotheists following Islam. So do all Islam worshiping people come under Netjar preview? Do Anubis have claim on them after death? What about people worshiping some Netjar - like maybe Horus - but not acknowleging Anubis as their Death God, only Osiris. Would they come under jurisdiction of Anubis, even contrary to their belief?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T18:33:16-08:00","id":1474671,"title":"","content":"@Glamourwaever pointed me on Discord -<br /> '(...)many Egyptian Muslim and Coptic Christians likely (in the context of the World) maintain cultural practices that tie them to the Netjeru even if religious hardliners object to those customs.' - <br /> <br /> So 'godly jurisdiction' runs counter to your own personal beliefs - CUSTOMS are the key here. You still can be monotheist and belive in One God, but went to Anubis control in death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T18:36:07-08:00","id":1474672,"title":"","content":"I would not. In the Pagan community, race being tied to gods or worship is associated with some very bad actors, and you risk, at best, being lumped into such a category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T18:51:01-08:00","id":1474674,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't handle it using ethnicity or geography; I'd handle it using worship. Think of it as a very mild form of Fatebinding: if you become actively involved in the Netjer religion, then your fate gets bound to that Pantheon and when you die, your soul goes to its Underworld. If your fate gets bound up with multiple Pantheons, well, that's one reason why the Pantheons have Gods of the Dead: if the Theoi and Netjer both have claims on your soul, then Hades and Anubis get to negotiate over which one gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T02:10:56-08:00","id":1474714,"title":"","content":"I think the thematic of Scion would go against the idea of Ethinicity or Geography limitations.<br /> <br /> It's far more probable that when the person dies they go to ALL the underworlds, I mean, you can find the person spirit in any underworld you look for it, because thats what one or more of the myths would expect. It makes no sense to me that THE GOD OF DEATH has control only over the dead that believe in him, in that casa the best option is believe in Jesus and go to heaven... best option in the long run at least.<br /> <br /> Human's beliefs are not relevant in that, only gods really define what happens, it would also explain why all Scions with Death purview see the spirits, and would allow the spirit to look and behave as expected for the spirit of the dead in to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T05:42:09-08:00","id":1474727,"title":"","content":"I would not do that. It\u2019s who you worship that counts, not your ethnic background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T06:29:57-08:00","id":1474733,"title":"","content":"Okay, but then I have almost <b>Origin</b> corebook example in game. Book says us that in canon/vanilla World setting, many people are worshiping both Abrahamic One God ( for Christians, Jews or Muslims ) <b>and</b> paying respects to Pantheons, like catholic priests in Vatican doing rites to Mars or Jupiter, from time to time.<br /> <br /> So, for example, we have Egyptian Muslim - he believes in Allah strongly, but pays respects to Osiris as lord of the Dead, because of family tradition. ( But NOT worshipping Anubis, as thinking him as lower god to Osiris. )<br /> <br /> <b>After death, our Egyptian Muslim goes to?</b><br /> 1. <b>Allah angel related to dead</b> - as he is still mainly Muslim.<br /> 2. <b>Osiris</b> - cause he believed in him as Lord of the Dead whole his life.<br /> 3. <b>Anubis</b> - as Osiris is putting dead in the day-to-day care for Anubis, by myths ( against belifes of our particular Egyptian ) <br /> <br /> How do you think about it?<br /> <br /> Also - this rise the added question of <b>if Abrahamic afterlife is real in Scion's World - and if even Abrahamic Pantheon exists?</b> ( Even if devs do not want to write it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <b>Is Abrahamic Pantheon even competition in those examples of mixed religion worshippers?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T06:52:24-08:00","id":1474735,"title":"","content":"My head-Canon is that an Abrahamic \u201cPantheon\u201d <i>does</i> exist, even if not detailed in any official material (though I have that in quotes because with the advent of Dragon and Masks of the Mythos, I'm debating whether Abrahamic concepts should be forced into the same mold as the Pantheons or if Legend should be replaced by a more suitable power stat; but that's something to be debated elsewhere), and that the Abrahamic gatekeeper(s?) for the souls of the dead would be involved in deciding the fate of a person's soul. With that in mind, my answer to \u201cwhere does the soul of the Egyptian Muslim go?\u201d is that the respective Abrahamic and Netjer psychopomps responsible for dealing with the souls of the dead would decide that among themselves on a case by case basis. There is no automated resolution to this; it's something that the respective \u201cGods of the Underworld\u201d need to work out among themselves: who has the stronger claim on this soul? <br /> <br /> That is, after all, a basic truth of the Scion setting: the Gods run reality; and how reality works is through the will of the Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T13:37:08-08:00","id":1474757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474733#post1474733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but then I have almost <b>Origin</b> corebook example in game. Book says us that in canon/vanilla World setting, many people are worshiping both Abrahamic One God ( for Christians, Jews or Muslims ) <b>and</b> paying respects to Pantheons, like catholic priests in Vatican doing rites to Mars or Jupiter, from time to time.<br /> <br /> So, for example, we have Egyptian Muslim - he believes in Allah strongly, but pays respects to Osiris as lord of the Dead, because of family tradition. ( But NOT worshipping Anubis, as thinking him as lower god to Osiris. )<br /> <br /> <b>After death, our Egyptian Muslim goes to?</b><br /> 1. <b>Allah angel related to dead</b> - as he is still mainly Muslim.<br /> 2. <b>Osiris</b> - cause he believed in him as Lord of the Dead whole his life.<br /> 3. <b>Anubis</b> - as Osiris is putting dead in the day-to-day care for Anubis, by myths ( against belifes of our particular Egyptian )<br /> <br /> How do you think about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone pointed out in the exact same question you posed in the Facebook group where you posed this exact same question, where ever their <i>FAITH</i> lies determines the underworld someone goes to.<br /> <br /> If someone is a devout, life-long Muslim who will give <i>respect</i> to others' faith in the Netjer, that doesn't mean they suddenly get bamf'd to Duat when they die. It means they likely still go to the Muslim ideal of Heaven as their underworld. Or maybe they get to choose. All I know is if I spent my whole life worshipping Allah and wound up in Duat, I'd be very confused.<br /> <br /> Also, I shouldn't need to point out that not all Muslims are Middle Eastern or North African. You really need to remove ethnicity from belief/faith because it is a very narrow view of how the <i>actual</i> world operates. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T15:45:56-08:00","id":1474762,"title":"","content":"In fairness, he did specify &quot;Egyptian Muslim&quot;, to reflect that he was asking about the fate of someone from the homeland of the Netjer but the faith of Allah - I didn't read it as &quot;all Muslims in general&quot;. We are talking about a fictional world with multiple long-lived faiths that are mostly inactive in our world - some unusual interactions and contradictions are inevitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T20:26:42-08:00","id":1474836,"title":"","content":"The impression I get is that it'd be possible for our Egyptian Muslim to end up in Duat (or for a Greek Christian to end up in Elysium, or w/e), but that the default assumption of the story is that if this were to happen, it would indicate that something had gone terribly wrong, and is not the proper course of events. Ending up in an afterlife outside of your faith would imply some sort of meddling from supernatural sources, and while you might get something like, &quot;Look, Bob, I know you were expecting the Pearly Gates but your family's been in my good graces for a thousand years and you did burn an offering for me that one time when you were eight; I can send you back to The World if you can do a solid for me. No other strings attached, and you can see St. Peter next time you step into traffic,&quot; you might also have rulers of the dead drawing in the dead of a rival pantheon--or deflecting their own away--for some reason.<br /> <br /> Other folks have pointed out the very real and real-world dangers of lashing ethnic identity too tightly to a religion. There's stories to be told, but they need to be handled with the right spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T07:08:49-08:00","id":1474844,"title":"","content":"There is probably a lot more religious syncretism in The World than we see, so someone who is a devout member of one faith but is part of a cultural tradition that still offers some worship or acknowledgement of Anubis in his role as a judge of the dead may encounter him after death where he judges if they are worthy. They'll still go onto to whatever afterlife is appropriate, not Duat. Anubis just effectively has a minor mantle that is part of their religious tradition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 02-17-2022, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T07:51:46-08:00","id":1474849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474836#post1474836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I get is that it'd be possible for our Egyptian Muslim to end up in Duat (or for a Greek Christian to end up in Elysium, or w/e), but that the default assumption of the story is that if this were to happen, it would indicate that something had gone terribly wrong, and is not the proper course of events. Ending up in an afterlife outside of your faith would imply some sort of meddling from supernatural sources, and while you might get something like, &quot;Look, Bob, I know you were expecting the Pearly Gates but your family's been in my good graces for a thousand years and you did burn an offering for me that one time when you were eight; I can send you back to The World if you can do a solid for me. No other strings attached, and you can see St. Peter next time you step into traffic,&quot; you might also have rulers of the dead drawing in the dead of a rival pantheon--or deflecting their own away--for some reason.<br /> <br /> Other folks have pointed out the very real and real-world dangers of lashing ethnic identity too tightly to a religion. There's stories to be told, but they need to be handled with the right spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see valkyries coming to collect or at least offer to collect someone who died in battle, not because they were a follower, but because Odin and Freya want a bunch of warriors on their side when Ragnarok comes.<br /> <br /> Incarnations of various gods probably try to arrange things for mortals they cared about too, possibly arranging for them to go to a different afterlife than the mortal wanted or expected to go to (which can be a neat plot hook, descending into your pantheon underworld to retrieve the soul of a mortal parent and send them to their preferred afterlife).<br /> <br /> It's also Scion, all myths are true. Entirely possible to have someone go to every afterlife all at once. The soul isn't a homogenous concept across cultures and time, but all concepts of it are true all at once in The World. If a sailor died in a naval battle you might find them in Fiddler's Green forever after, dining in the hall of \u00c6gir with other drowned men, being punished in hell for their life of sin, wandering the Asphodel Meadows, and reincarnated into a new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T05:45:29-08:00","id":1474894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474733#post1474733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, but then I have almost <b>Origin</b> corebook example in game. Book says us that in canon/vanilla World setting, many people are worshiping both Abrahamic One God ( for Christians, Jews or Muslims ) <b>and</b> paying respects to Pantheons, like catholic priests in Vatican doing rites to Mars or Jupiter, from time to time.<br /> <br /> So, for example, we have Egyptian Muslim - he believes in Allah strongly, but pays respects to Osiris as lord of the Dead, because of family tradition. ( But NOT worshipping Anubis, as thinking him as lower god to Osiris. )<br /> <br /> <b>After death, our Egyptian Muslim goes to?</b><br /> 1. <b>Allah angel related to dead</b> - as he is still mainly Muslim.<br /> 2. <b>Osiris</b> - cause he believed in him as Lord of the Dead whole his life.<br /> 3. <b>Anubis</b> - as Osiris is putting dead in the day-to-day care for Anubis, by myths ( against belifes of our particular Egyptian )<br /> <br /> How do you think about it?<br /> <br /> Also - this rise the added question of <b>if Abrahamic afterlife is real in Scion's World - and if even Abrahamic Pantheon exists?</b> ( Even if devs do not want to write it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <b>Is Abrahamic Pantheon even competition in those examples of mixed religion worshippers?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The question of what cosmology applies to people who follow several religious traditions is always a very interesting one, not just but especially in the context of Scion. This doesn't just apply to the overlap with the Abrahamic - what about, for example, an ancient Roman who honours both Iuppiter and Isis? My personal take on that is that the question kind of resolves itself, because the soul or whatever it is that enters into the afterlife is itself an aspect of the cosmology. So our hypothetical Roman has both a Dei-affiliated soul that may become a <i>lar</i> and a Netjeru-affiliated soul that will enter the Duat. Does that make sense?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T07:24:12-08:00","id":1474900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474894#post1474894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question of what cosmology applies to people who follow several religious traditions is always a very interesting one, not just but especially in the context of Scion. This doesn't just apply to the overlap with the Abrahamic - what about, for example, an ancient Roman who honours both Iuppiter and Isis? My personal take on that is that the question kind of resolves itself, because the soul or whatever it is that enters into the afterlife is itself an aspect of the cosmology. So our hypothetical Roman has both a Dei-affiliated soul that may become a <i>lar</i> and a Netjeru-affiliated soul that will enter the Duat. Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically my suggestion, but ao expand to other beliefs as well.<br /> <br /> If you know a person died sometime ago, just go to you favorite underworld and use the proper techniques to summon the spirits and you will find the desired spirit in the way it is expected for that place.<br /> <br /> Any other approach would make a myth not true, and so it would not fit the idea of all myths are true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T13:44:12-08:00","id":1474922,"title":"","content":"Eh. I still say that a person needs to somehow be connected to a particular mythology before their soul ends up in its Underworld. Plus, the idea that it only ends up in <i>one</i> leads to tension and drama, which is good for storytelling; the idea that your soul ends up in all of them is kind of like the notion of Quantum Immortality: if every possible fate is going to be realized, then what's the point of striving for one fate or trying to avoid another?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-19-2022, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T23:38:55-08:00","id":1474947,"title":"","content":"<b>I will probably go with 2 notions in my World interpretation</b>:<br /> 1. Many Underworlds exists and Gods of Death need to haggle between them, resolving 'bureaucratic conflicts' about particular soul.<br /> <br /> 2. Abrahamic Pantheon(s) exists ( made by higher angels ), but after dominating Western world in Middle Ages, they kinda stop fighting for each soul as by Europe, Middle East and Americas - they have like over half of humans population ( now <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Religion#Demographical_classification\" target=\"_blank\">Christianity has circa 33%, Islam has 23%</a> ). They rather do not struggle over each soul, that odd exception that could go two different Underworlds. Most of the time, all is needed is to talk with Abrahamic psychopomp and show they soul was connected to old Pantheon, in some meaningful way.<br /> <br /> Asking Scions of Gods of Death to help with those 'soul disputes' is typical small quests for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2022, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T09:35:55-08:00","id":1474981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474900#post1474900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically my suggestion, but ao expand to other beliefs as well.<br /> <br /> If you know a person died sometime ago, just go to you favorite underworld and use the proper techniques to summon the spirits and you will find the desired spirit in the way it is expected for that place.<br /> <br /> Any other approach would make a myth not true, and so it would not fit the idea of all myths are true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, true. Didn't mean to detract from what you said, just saw that question, was immediately intrigued, and failed to read all of what everyone else had posted. Guess it's a case of &quot;same hat&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","user":"Sacerdos","date":". 02-19-2022, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:12:37-08:00","id":1474984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sacerdos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474669-pantheons-ethnicities?p=1474981#post1474981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, true. Didn't mean to detract from what you said, just saw that question, was immediately intrigued, and failed to read all of what everyone else had posted. Guess it's a case of &quot;same hat&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was not criticizing, when the post is active hardly we can read all. But it\u2019s good to see others coming with the same idea\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T07:09:34-07:00","id":1476725,"title":"","content":"I run today story with Abrahamic Pantheon. I run that Angels makes complaint form and then sends you to House That Makes You Mad to resolve the complaint. But fantastical is that in Scion World, you <b>can</b> get soul back, before you get mad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. <b>Scions from Sh\u00e9n </b>would be best to solve those Mad House complaints - with all those experiance with Celestial Bureaucracy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JtEkUmYecnk\" data-code=\"JtEkUmYecnk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JtEkUmYecnk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-19-2022, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T10:30:04-07:00","id":1476980,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily geographical or ethnic I'd say it more ties to either one's own faith, as being a part of a creed would be a viable reason to tie you to its fate, barring incidents where a portfolio overlap occurs. To use a fictitious god as the overlap because my brain is not working great with the real stuff; The Empty Wind, god of the forgotten dead, has the portfolio so anyone who dies who would be completely unknown and unmourned outside just being a dead person could show up to reap anyone regardless of faith who fits those criteria due to them being part of its domain. That said if you were a devout follower of Loa that wouldn't be denied the afterlife of their own faith, the deceased would just potentially end up with options on where to go for their end. Or you could go with the idea of them going to different places, but with claims and ties elsewhereas needed. I'm just spitballing the idea there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}